<!--
    The app's own high contrast (Theme setting "High contrast", owner round 5 #5), merged over Dark by AppTheme only while
    that setting is on and Windows is not in a contrast theme (a Windows contrast theme wins). WinUI's control keys alias
    its base brushes at load time, so overriding a base brush does not reach the controls (measured): this lists the
    control keys of the controls Mandrill uses, plus the app's own keys. States follow Windows high contrast: hover,
    press and selection are the highlight with black text. Colours are "Night sky"-like (lead-approved), the only colour
    literals in the app besides Themes/ExplorerItems.xaml and MandrillMainInstructionBrush in Themes/Brushes.xaml; contrast on black: text 21:1, focus 19.6:1, highlight 14.4:1
    (black text on it 14.4:1), disabled 5.3:1, grey 8.6:1 (black text on it 8.6:1). Disabled is a mid grey, not Night
    sky's green: a disabled button must look subdued, never brighter than an enabled one (owner round 6 #8).
-->
